if(B.b.l(q,"what is protein")||q==="explain protein"||q==="protein")return A.c0(B.h,"Biochemical Structure & Composition:\nProteins are linear polymers of amino acids joined by covalent peptide bonds. Of the 20 standard proteinogenic amino acids, 9 are essential (EAAs: histidine, isoleucine, leucine, lysine, methionine, phenylalanine, threonine, tryptophan, valine) and must be obtained through dietary sources.\n\nPhysiological Roles:\n\u2022 Structural Scaffolding: Actin, myosin, and collagen maintain musculoskeletal integrity.\n\u2022 Enzymatic Catalysis: Nearly all metabolic reactions depend on functional protein enzymes.\n\u2022 Peptide Hormones & Immunity: Insulin, glucagon, and immunoglobulins regulate systemic homeostasis and pathogen defense.\n\u2022 Nitrogen Balance: Net muscle balance depends on the continuous dynamic flux between muscle protein synthesis (MPS) and muscle protein breakdown (MPB). Leucine acts as the primary molecular trigger stimulating the mTORC1 signaling cascade.",B.Y,B.P3,s,B.ht,"Protein: Essential Biological Macromolecule for Cellular Architecture and Enzyme Function",s,s,s,B.WI,s,r,a,"Target high-biological-value protein sources distributed evenly across 3\u20134 daily meals to optimize muscle protein synthesis (MPS) and metabolic satiety.","GEN-PROTEIN-2026",B.bO,"Nutrient Earth synthesizes validated scientific literature for educational purposes. Individual medical conditions (e.g. chronic kidney disease) require tailored clinical nephrology supervision.",s,s)
if(B.b.l(q,"carbohydrate")||B.b.l(q,"what is carb")||q==="explain carbs")return A.c0(B.h,"Molecular Classification:\nCarbohydrates (C_n(H2O)_n) span monosaccharides (glucose, fructose, galactose), disaccharides (sucrose, lactose, maltose), oligosaccharides, and polysaccharides (starch, glycogen, cellulose, pectin).\n\nMetabolic Energy Kinetics:\nDigestible carbohydrates hydrolyze into glucose, stimulating pancreatic beta-cell insulin secretion and facilitating GLUT4 translocation into skeletal muscle and hepatic tissues for ATP generation or glycogen storage.\n\nPrebiotic Fiber & Microbiome Axis:\nNon-digestible fibers bypass small-intestinal digestion to reach the colon, where anaerobic commensal microbiota ferment them into short-chain fatty acids (SCFAs: acetate, propionate, butyrate). Butyrate fuels colonocytes, fortifies gut barrier integrity, and suppresses systemic low-grade inflammation.",B.Y,B.Oz,s,B.ht,"Carbohydrates: Primary Cellular Fuel and Digestive Fiber Matrices",s,s,s,B.Zx,s,r,a,"Prioritize intact, complex carbohydrates rich in viscous and fermentable prebiotic fiber to stabilize postprandial glucose curves and nourish colonic microflora.","GEN-CARBS-2026",B.bO,"Nutrient Earth provides nutritional biochemistry syntheses for general education; does not replace individualized diabetes medical nutrition therapy.",s,s)
if(B.b.l(q,"sleep recovery")||B.b.l(q,"what is sleep recovery")||q==="sleep recovery")return A.c0(B.h,"Sleep Architecture & Physical Restoration:\nHuman sleep cycles through Non-Rapid Eye Movement (NREM N1, N2, N3) and Rapid Eye Movement (REM) every ~90 minutes. N3 Slow-Wave Sleep (SWS) is the primary restorative stage during which the pituitary gland secretes up to 70% of daily pulsatile growth hormone (GH), orchestrating cellular repair, amino acid uptake, and glycogen synthesis.\n\nGlymphatic Neuro-Metabolic Clearance:\nDuring deep sleep, the brain\u2019s interstitial space expands by up to 60%, permitting convective cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) flow through the astrocytic AQP4 water channels. This glymphatic system clears neurotoxic metabolic debris, including amyloid-beta and tau proteins.\n\nCircadian Chronobiology:\nThe suprachiasmatic nucleus (SCN) coordinates pineal melatonin synthesis under low-lux darkness, reducing nocturnal core body temperature by ~0.5\u20131\xb0C and initiating parasympathetic recovery.",B.Y,B.Ox,s,B.ht,"Sleep Recovery: Neuro-Anabolic Restoration and Glymphatic Clearance",s,s,s,B.ZR,s,r,a,"Maintain strict circadian timing with consistent wake times and light exposure to optimize slow-wave sleep (SWS) depth and nocturnal growth hormone release.","GEN-SLEEP-2026",B.bc,"Nutrient Earth sleep analyses are educational; clinical sleep apnea or chronic insomnia requires physician evaluation and polysomnography.",s,s)
if(B.b.l(q,"what are vitamins")||q==="explain vitamins"||q==="vitamins")return A.c0(B.h,"Biochemical Definition & Classification:\nVitamins are organic compounds required by the human organism in microgram or milligram quantities that cannot be synthesized endogenously in adequate amounts. They are categorized into two fundamental biochemical classes:\n\n1. Water-Soluble Vitamins (Vitamin C and the B-Complex: B1, B2, B3, B5, B6, B7, B9, B12):\nFunction primarily as coenzymes in cellular bioenergetics (Krebs cycle, oxidative phosphorylation), DNA methylation, and antioxidant defense. Excess quantities are generally cleared renally.\n\n2. Fat-Soluble Vitamins (A, D, E, K):\nRequire dietary lipids and biliary micellar packaging for intestinal absorption. Stored in adipose tissue and the liver. Vitamin D acts as a genomic secosteroid hormone modulating over 1,000 genes; Vitamin K regulates osteocalcin carboxylation and vascular Matrix Gla Protein (MGP) activation.",B.Y,B.Ow,s,B.ht,"Vitamins: Essential Organic Micronutrients for Enzyme Co-Factor Activity and Genomic Regulation",s,s,s,B.ZF,s,r,a,"Prioritize a colorful, nutrient-dense diet across diverse plant and animal whole foods to supply full-spectrum micronutrients and bio-enhancing synergistic co-factors.","GEN-VITAMINS-2026",B.bO,"Nutrient Earth provides nutritional science education; megadosing fat-soluble vitamins can accumulate in adipose tissue and cause hypervitaminosis.",s,s)
if(B.b.l(q,"ayurveda")||B.b.l(q,"explain ayurveda")||q==="what is ayurveda")return A.c0(B.h,'Philosophical & Classical Foundations:\nAyurveda ("the science of life") is one of the world\'s oldest codifications of individualized medicine, formalized in classical texts including the Charaka Samhita and Sushruta Samhita under the governance of the Ministry of AYUSH, Government of India.\n\nThe Tridosha Framework & Bio-Physiology:\n\u2022 Vata (Kinetic/Neuro-endocrinological): Governs cellular division, motility, and neurological impulse transmission.\n\u2022 Pitta (Metabolic/Bio-transformative): Controls enzymatic digestion, thermo-genesis, and hepatic transformation.\n\u2022 Kapha (Structural/Anabolic): Regulates fluid homeostasis, lubrication, and immune architecture.\n\nAgni & Ama Concept:\nAyurvedic physiology prioritizes Agni (the central metabolic/digestive fire). Impaired Agni produces Ama (undigested metabolic endotoxins), which contemporary science translates to sub-clinical endotoxemia and systemic inflammatory cascade.\n\nModern Integrative Pharmacognosy:\nBotanical therapeutics from the Ayurvedic pharmacopoeia (e.g. Curcuma longa/Turmeric, Withania somnifera/Ashwagandha, Plantago ovata/Isabgol) are increasingly validated by peer-reviewed clinical trials demonstrating adaptogenic, anti-inflammatory, and prebiotic properties.',B.Y,B.OI,s,B.ht,"Ayurveda: Traditional Indian Medicine System and Individualized Bio-Constitution (Prakriti)",s,s,s,B.XA,s,r,a,"Incorporate evidenced Ayurvedic principles of circadian eating rhythm (Dinacharya) and digestive capacity (Agni) into contemporary lifestyle frameworks.","GEN-AYURVEDA-2026",B.bc,"Nutrient Earth presents Ayurvedic literature in scientific translation for educational wellness; it does not replace diagnosis or care by licensed AYUSH medical practitioners.",s,s)
